		<wp:meta_key><![CDATA[book_description]]></wp:meta_key>
		<wp:meta_value><![CDATA[Published in 1934, *Cheliyala Katta* is one of Viswanadha Sathyanarayana's most profound psychological and social novels. The title metaphorically translates to "The Seawall" or "The Shore Line" that holds back raging oceanic waves, representing social boundaries, moral integrity, and traditional values protecting society from chaos.

Set against the backdrop of modernizing India, the novel delves deep into the emotional and psychological conflicts of its characters, contrasting traditional Eastern values of restraint and societal duty with Western individualistic ideals. Through intricate character studies, Viswanadha explores how breaking moral boundaries impacts family structures and individual peace, emphasizing that self-discipline (*Dharma*) serves as the ultimate safeguard for human civilization.]]></wp:meta_value>
		</wp:postmeta>
